# Verilog style (lowRISC)

Follow [VERILOG_STYLE.md](../../VERILOG_STYLE.md) and the [lowRISC guide](https://github.com/lowRISC/style-guides/blob/master/VerilogCodingStyle.md).

## Quick checklist

- `UpperCamelCase` module parameters with types (`parameter int unsigned Width = 8`)
- `lower_snake_case` signals; ports use `_i` / `_o` / `rst_ni`
- `logic` + `always_ff` / `always_comb`; 2-space indent
- FSM: `typedef enum logic [...] { StIdle, ... } foo_e`; `_q` / `_d` registers; `unique case`
- Explicit literal widths; no tabs; no trailing whitespace
- Hand-written sources use `.sv`; wizard IP stays `.v` (`*_fifo.v`, `pll_100mhz.v`)
- Keep project file headers; do not edit Quartus wizard IP

## Example port list

```systemverilog
module foo #(
  parameter int unsigned Width = 8
) (
  input  logic             clk_i,
  input  logic             rst_ni,
  input  logic [Width-1:0] data_i,
  output logic [Width-1:0] data_o
);
```

## Instantiating migrated children

Use matching port names; map legacy parent ports explicitly:

```systemverilog
memory_fetcher #(.TotalRowWidth(TOTAL_ROW_WIDTH)) u_fetch (
  .clk_i    (clk),
  .rst_ni   (reset_n),
  .mem_req_o(mem_req)
);
```
